ht","regular"],"width":["regular"],"x_height":["regular"]},"description":"Long since replaced by computers, the popular Wrico mechanical lettering kits used by draftsmen and amateur sign makers in the 60s and 70s served as the inspiration for the Bryant family of typefaces. Well-suited for a range of tasks, the Bryant fonts are a warm and modern take on the geometric sans serif.","foundry":"Process Type Foundry","lastModified":1645751470352,"name":"Bryant Alternate","variations":["n3","n4","n5","n7"],"web_link":"http://typekit.com/fonts/bryant-web-alternate"},{"id":"nfhc","__v":0,"browse_info":{"capitals":["uppercase-lowercase"],"classification":["sans-serif"],"contrast":["low"],"language":["ca","cs","de","en","es","fr","hu","it","mt","nl","pl","pt","sl","sv","tr"],"number_style":["uppercase"],"recommended_for":[],"weight":["light","regular"],"width":["condensed"],"x_height":["regular"]},"description":"Designed for situations where large point sizes and maximum letter count need to coexist, Bryant Compressed is the narrowest of the triple-width Bryant series. Sharp stem joins and increased contrast – stylistic departures from the other weights and widths – allow this font to preserve the warm Bryant tone while remaining narrow in width.","foundry":"Process Type Foundry","lastModified":1645751470343,"name":"Bryant Compressed","variations":["n3","n4","n5","n7"],"web_link":"http://typekit.com/fonts/bryant-web-compressed"},{"id":"rlcb","__v":0,"browse_info":{"capitals":["uppercase-lowercase"],"classification":["sans-serif"],"contrast":["low"],"language":["ca","cs","de","en","es","fr","hu","it","mt","nl","pl","pt","sl","sv","tr"],"number_style":["uppercase"],"recommended_for":[],"weight":["light","regular"],"width":["condensed"],"x_height":["regular"]},"description":"Of the three Bryant widths, Bryant Condensed is the middle member of the series. Exuding the same warm demeanor popularized by its big brother Bryant, this family of condensed fonts is a simple collection of