ull,"foundry":"Dave Rowland","lastModified":1673053878085,"name":"Chill Script","variations":["n4"],"web_link":"http://typekit.com/fonts/chill-script"},{"id":"rxvl","__v":0,"browse_info":{"capitals":["uppercase-lowercase"],"classification":["handmade"],"contrast":[],"language":["en","es","nl","pt","sv"],"number_style":["uppercase"],"recommended_for":[],"weight":["regular"],"width":["regular"],"x_height":["regular"]},"description":null,"foundry":"Fonthead","lastModified":1588840819708,"name":"Chinchilla","variations":["n4","n6"],"web_link":"http://typekit.com/fonts/chinchilla"},{"id":"pfcv","__v":0,"browse_info":{"capitals":["all-or-small-caps"],"classification":["decorative"],"contrast":[],"language":["de","en","es","fr","it","nl","pt","sv"],"number_style":["uppercase"],"recommended_for":[],"weight":["regular"],"width":["regular"],"x_height":[]},"description":"A marvellous idea for a font that was inspired by stenciled lettering on imported merchandise containers. Chinese Rocks looks like it was a hand cut rubber stamp, used about a million times. Uneven line thickness and odd stem widths combine with sharp corners to create the effect of letters cut out with a box knife in a hurry.","foundry":"Typodermic","lastModified":1588840819688,"name":"Chinese Rocks","variations":["n4"],"web_link":"http://typekit.com/fonts/chinese-rocks"},{"id":"wyrn","__v":0,"browse_info":{"capitals":["all-or-small-caps"],"classification":["decorative"],"contrast":["low"],"language":["ca","de","en","es","fr","it","nl","pt","sv"],"number_style":["uppercase"],"recommended_for":[],"weight":["regular"],"width":["regular"],"x_height":[]},"description":"Greetings from Chippewa Falls, home of Wisconsin’s finest natural spring water. It’s an old-fashioned kinda place, so lost in time, they don't know about sparkling water or mineral water. “Never heard of water with bubbles. Where does that come from?” wonder the locals. “All we have here is Chippewa water.”\r\nIn the spirit of the old days, before water sparkled and before typefaces were known as fonts, Chank is proud to introduce Chippewa Falls the font. This font comes with fancy swirly uppercase letters and stout small caps for lowercase, as well as a heart-warming story. Chank rescued this former custom font from an abandoned design proposal. He gave it some TLC and before long a retro typeface emerged, with lettering worthy of good old fashioned sleigh rides and candy canes.\r\n\r\nEnjoy this font as you would a cup of hot cocoa next to a potbelly stove on a snowy day.","foundry":"Chank Co","lastModified":1588840819706,"name":"Chippewa Falls","variations":["n5"],"web_link":"http://typekit.com/fonts/chippewa-falls"},{"id":"zhbz","__v":0,"browse_info":{"capitals":["uppercase-lowercase"],"classification":["sans-serif"],"contrast":["high"],"language":["ca","de","en","es","fr","it","nl","pt","sv"],"number_style":["uppercase"],"recommended_for":[],"weight":["regular"],"width":["regular"],"x_height":["regular"]},"description":null,"foundry":"Google","is_personal":false,"lastModified":1734108733254,"name":"Chivo","variations":["n1","i1","n2","i2","n3","i3","n4","i4","n6","i6","n7","i7","n8","i8","n9","i9"],"web_link":"http://fonts.adobe.com/fonts/chivo"},{"id":"hmds","__v":0,"browse_info":{"capitals":[],"classification":[],"contrast":[],"language":[],"number_style":[],"recommended_for":[],"weight":[],"width":[],"x_height":[]},"description":null,"foundry":"Google","lastModified":1704935483940,"name":"Chivo Mono","variations":["n1","i1","n2","i2","n3","i3","n4","i4","n5","i5","n6","i6","n7","i7","n8","i8","n9","i9"],"web_link":"http://typekit.com/fonts/chivo-mono"},{"id":"pmhb","__v":0,"browse_info":{"capitals":[],"classification":[],"contrast":[],"language":[],"number_style":[],"recommended_for":[],"weight":[],"width":[],"x_height":[]},"description":null,"foundry":"Josh Ownby","is_personal":false,"lastModified":1759189885409,"name":"Chloe","variations":["n4"],"web_link":"http://fonts.adobe.com/fonts/chloe"},{"id"