o see it used as Hagrid’s handwriting in the Harry Potter books.\r\n\r\nIt’s my own handwriting carefully digitized by hand (not auto-traced). Handwriting fonts are very common now, but they weren’t in 1989. I did it just to see what it would look like, never dreaming that other people might want to use it. (Thank you, Mark Solsburg of FontHaus.)\r\n\r\nTwo new weights—Bold and Heavy—were added in 2003.\r\n\r\nFirst released in 1992.","foundry":"Mark Simonson Studio","lastModified":1588840820829,"name":"Felt Tip Roman","variations":["n4","n7","n8"],"web_link":"http://typekit.com/fonts/felt-tip-roman"},{"id":"bcpv","__v":0,"browse_info":{"capitals":["uppercase-lowercase"],"classification":["handmade"],"contrast":["regular"],"language":["ca","cs","de","en","es","fr","hu","it","mt","nl","pl","pt","sl","sv","tr"],"number_style":["uppercase"],"recommended_for":[],"weight":["regular"],"width":["regular"],"x_height":["regular"]},"description":"This typeface is a faithful rendering of my father’s handwriting, which of course, had a big influence on my own handwriting, now immortalized in Felt Tip Roman. Originally created as a gift; release to the market with permission.","foundry":"Mark Simonson Studio","lastModified":1588840820842,"name":"Felt Tip Senior","variations":["n4"],"web_link":"http://typekit.com/fonts/felt-tip-senior"},{"id":"xpwg","__v":0,"browse_info":{"capitals":["uppercase-lowercase"],"classification":["handmade"],"contrast":["regular"],"language":["ca","cs","de","en","es","fr","hu","it","mt","nl","pl","pt","sl","sv","tr"],"number_style":["uppercase"],"recommended_for":[],"weight":["regular"],"width":["regular"],"x_height":["regular"]},"description":"Felt Tip Woman (2003) is based on the handwriting of graphic designer Patricia Thompson. The name was inspired by a misunderstanding: Pat was working with the editor of a children’s book journal when she noticed that some type in one of the books they were reviewing was set in Felt Tip Roman. She pointed this ou