"},{"id":"ffht","__v":0,"browse_info":{"capitals":["uppercase-lowercase"],"classification":["sans-serif"],"contrast":["regular"],"language":["ca","cs","de","en","es","fr","hu","it","mt","nl","pl","pt","sl","sv","tr"],"number_style":["uppercase"],"recommended_for":["headings"],"weight":["heavy","light","regular"],"width":["condensed"],"x_height":["high"]},"description":"FF Dax Compact is an extension of the FF Dax family. The main difference is that ascenders and descenders are relatively small and the upper case letters have the same height as the lower case letters with ascenders. That makes the typeface appear larger and more compact although set in the same point size. The FF Dax Compact is especially suitable for headlines in magazines, newspapers, for posters, flyers ... whenever a little more noise is needed. Designed by Hans Reichel.","foundry":"FontFont","lastModified":1588840820941,"name":"FF Dax Compact Pro","variations":["n3","n4","n6","n7","n8","n9"],"web_link":"http://typekit.com/fonts/ff-dax-compact-web-pro"},{"id":"dbqg","__v":0,"browse_info":{"capitals":["uppercase-lowercase"],"classification":["sans-serif"],"contrast":["regular"],"language":["ca","cs","de","el","en","es","fr","hu","it","mt","nl","pl","pt","ru","sl","sv","tr"],"number_style":["uppercase"],"recommended_for":["headings"],"weight":["heavy","light","regular"],"width":["regular"],"x_height":["high"]},"description":"FF Dax is a wider version of FF Dax Condensed. The FF Dax family developed from the idea of combining the clarity of a narrow Futura with a “slightly roman touch”. The result is a space-saving but very legible typeface of timeless design. Designed by Hans Reichel.","foundry":"FontFont","lastModified":1588840820950,"name":"FF Dax Pro","variations":["n3","i3","n4","i4","n6","i6","n7","i7","n8","i8","n9","i9"],"web_link":"http://typekit.com/fonts/ff-dax-web-pro"},{"id":"xjff","__v":0,"browse_info":{"capitals":["uppercase-lowercase"],"classification":["sans-serif"],"contrast":["reg