onts/ff-speak-web"},{"id":"cmfb","__v":0,"browse_info":{"capitals":["uppercase-lowercase"],"classification":["serif"],"contrast":["high"],"language":["ca","cs","de","en","es","fr","hu","it","mt","nl","pl","pt","sl","sv","tr"],"number_style":["uppercase"],"recommended_for":[],"weight":["heavy","regular"],"width":["regular"],"x_height":["regular"]},"description":null,"foundry":"FontFont","lastModified":1588840821208,"name":"FF Spinoza Pro","variations":["n4","i4","n7","i7"],"web_link":"http://typekit.com/fonts/ff-spinoza-web-pro"},{"id":"xwmz","__v":0,"browse_info":{"capitals":["uppercase-lowercase"],"classification":["serif"],"contrast":["regular"],"language":["ca","cs","da","de","en","es","fr","hu","it","mt","nl","no","pl","pt","sl","sv","tr"],"number_style":["uppercase"],"recommended_for":["headings","paragraphs"],"weight":["regular"],"width":["regular"],"x_height":["regular"]},"description":"Mitja Miklavčič drew FF Tisa to meet the technological and aesthetic requirements of modern magazine use. His goal was to develop a softer, more dynamic version of a nineteenth-century slab serif wood type. A large x-height and pronounced serifs make FF Tisa extremely legible in text sizes and its unique design details and a fairly upright italic become evident in display applications. The typeface was selected by the TDC judges for a Certificate of Excellence in Type Design in 2007. ","foundry":"FontFont","lastModified":1588840821235,"name":"FF Tisa Pro","variations":["n1","i1","n3","i3","n4","i4","n6","i6","n7","i7","n8","i8","n9","i9"],"web_link":"http://typekit.com/fonts/ff-tisa-web-pro"},{"id":"lgpw","__v":0,"browse_info":{"capitals":["uppercase-lowercase"],"classification":["sans-serif"],"contrast":["regular"],"language":["ca","cs","de","en","es","fr","hu","it","mt","nl","pl","pt","ru","sl","sv","tr"],"number_style":["uppercase"],"recommended_for":["headings","paragraphs"],"weight":["heavy","light","regular"],"width":["regular"],"x_height":["regular"]},"description":"FF Tisa Sans\r\nFF Tisa Sans is Slovenian designer Mitja Miklavčič’s follow-up typeface to FF Tisa. Whether used together or separately, both of his families are excellent choices for branding projects and complex editorial applications. The original FF Tisa is one of the new-millennium favorites in the FontFont library. Upon its release, the typeface found its niche with print designers. But FF Tisa Web was a quick hit, too, and became a go-to selection for web designers the world over.","foundry":"FontFont","lastModified":1588840821248,"name":"FF Tisa Sans Pro","variations":["n1","i1","n3","i3","n4","i4","n5","i5","n7","i7","n8","i8","n9","i9"],"web_link":"http://typekit.com/fonts/ff-tisa-sans-web-pro"},{"id":"xxsq","__v":0,"browse_info":{"capitals":[],"classification":[],"contrast":[],"language":["ca","cs","de","en","es","fr","hu","it","mt","nl","pl","pt","sl","sv","tr"],"number_style":[],"recommended_for":[],"weight":[],"width":[],"x_height":[]},"description":null,"foundry":"FontFont","lastModified":1588840821228,"name":"FF Typestar OCR Pro","variations":["n4"],"web_link":"http://typekit.com/fonts/ff-typestar-ocr-web-pro"},{"id":"hrsz","__v":0,"browse_info":{"capitals":["uppercase-lowercase"],"classification":["sans-serif"],"contrast":["regular"],"language":["ca","de","en","es","fr","it","nl","pt","sv"],"number_style":["uppercase"],"recommended_for":[],"weight":["regular"],"width":["regular"],"x_height":["high"]},"description":"FF Typestar from eBoy is a collection of five unaffected fonts for the working world – the classic typewriter meeting the demands of modern communication. The four basic weights offer everything necessary for office communication and the OCR variation is a monospaced alternative for more mechanical moments. Designed by Steffen Sauerteig.\r\n\r\n","foundry":"FontFont","lastModified":1588840821245,"name":"FF Typestar Pro","variations":["n4","i4","n9","i9"],"web_link":"http://typekit.com/fonts/ff-typestar-web"},{"id":"tsxj","__v":0,"browse_info