rowse_info":{"capitals":["uppercase-lowercase"],"classification":["serif"],"contrast":["regular"],"language":["ca","cs","de","en","es","fr","hu","it","nl","pl","pt","sl","sv","tr"],"number_style":["uppercase"],"recommended_for":[],"weight":["heavy","regular"],"width":["regular"],"x_height":["high"]},"description":"Lapture is based on the Leipziger Antiqua by Albert Kapr, released in 1971 by the East German foundry Typoart. It has been digitized, extended and carefully redesigned by Tim Ahrens, preserving the warmth and rough texture of the original metal fonts. A unique feature of this font is the introduction of gothic shapes into a latin typeface. As Kapr explains, “the basic concept is to string together narrow white hexagons as counters and inter-letter spaces, defined by vertical stems and triangular serifs. The interior spaces are at least as important as the strokes that make up the characters.”","foundry":"Just Another Foundry","lastModified":1588840823169,"name":"JAF Lapture","variations":["n4","i4","n6","i6","n7","i7"],"web_link":"http://typekit.com/fonts/jaf-lapture"},{"id":"wyzn","__v":0,"browse_info":{"capitals":["uppercase-lowercase"],"classification":["serif"],"contrast":["regular"],"language":["ca","cs","de","en","es","fr","hu","it","nl","pl","pt","sl","sv","tr"],"number_style":["uppercase"],"recommended_for":[],"weight":["heavy","regular"],"width":["regular"],"x_height":["high"]},"description":"Lapture is based on the Leipziger Antiqua by Albert Kapr, released in 1971 by the East German foundry Typoart. It has been digitized, extended and carefully redesigned by Tim Ahrens, preserving the warmth and rough texture of the original metal fonts. A unique feature of this font is the introduction of gothic shapes into a latin typeface. As Kapr explains, “the basic concept is to string together narrow white hexagons as counters and inter-letter spaces, defined by vertical stems and triangular serifs. The interior spaces are at least as important as the strokes that make up the characters.”","foundry":"Just Another Foundry","lastModified":1588840823197,"name":"JAF Lapture Caption","variations":["n4","i4","n6","i6","n7","i7"],"web_link":"http://typekit.com/fonts/jaf-lapture-caption"},{"id":"cggc","__v":0,"browse_info":{"capitals":[],"classification":[],"contrast":[],"language":[],"number_style":[],"recommended_for":[],"weight":[],"width":[],"x_height":[]},"description":null,"foundry":"Just Another Foundry","is_personal":false,"lastModified":1758844287782,"name":"JAF Lapture Condensed","variations":["n4","n6","n7","n8","n9"],"web_link":"http://fonts.adobe.com/fonts/jaf-lapture-condensed"},{"id":"wtgg","__v":0,"browse_info":{"capitals":["uppercase-lowercase"],"classification":["serif"],"contrast":["high"],"language":["ca","cs","de","en","es","fr","hu","it","nl","pl","pt","sl","sv","tr"],"number_style":["uppercase"],"recommended_for":["headings"],"weight":["regular"],"width":["regular"],"x_height":["high"]},"description":null,"foundry":"Just Another Foundry","lastModified":1758844287795,"name":"JAF Lapture Display","variations":["n4","i4","n6","i6","n7","i7","n8","i8","n9","i9"],"web_link":"http://fonts.adobe.com/fonts/jaf-lapture-display"},{"id":"phtx","__v":0,"browse_info":{"capitals":["uppercase-lowercase"],"classification":["serif"],"contrast":["high"],"language":["ca","cs","de","en","es","fr","hu","it","nl","pl","pt","sl","sv","tr"],"number_style":["uppercase"],"recommended_for":[],"weight":["heavy","regular"],"width":["regular"],"x_height":["high"]},"description":"Lapture is based on the Leipziger Antiqua by Albert Kapr, released in 1971 by the East German foundry Typoart. It has been digitized, extended and carefully redesigned by Tim Ahrens, preserving the warmth and rough texture of the original metal fonts. A unique feature of this font is the introduction of gothic shapes into a latin typeface. As Kapr explains, “the basic concept is to string together narrow white hexagons as counters and inter-letter spaces, defined by vertical stems and triangular serifs. The interior spaces are at least as important as the strokes that make up the characters.”","foundry":"Just Another Foundry","lastModified":1588840823209,"name":"JAF Lapture Subhead","variations":["n4","i4","n6","i6","n7","i7"],"web_link":"http://typekit.com/fonts/jaf-lapture-subhead"},{"id":"vyjt","__v":0,"browse_info":{"capitals":["all-or-small-caps"],"classification":["decorative"],"contrast":["low"],"language":["ca","cs","de","en","es","fr","hu","it","nl","pl","pt","sl","sv","tr"],"number_style":["uppercase"],"recommended_for":[],"weight":["heavy","light","regular"],"width":["regular"],"x_height":[]},"description":"Although at first sight Mashine is a strict, “non-designed” typeface, this display font is not as geometric as it seems. The use of serif-like terminals and unusual joints gives the design a unique look. For most letters, stylistic alternates can be accessed by using lowercase or capital letters.","foundry":"Just Another Foundry","lastModified":1588840823201,"name":"JAF Mashine","variations":["n2","n3","n4","n6","n7","n8"],"web_link":"http://typekit.com/fonts/jaf-mashine"},{"id":"mhpd","__v":0,"browse_info":{"capitals":["all-or-small-caps"],"classification":["decorative"],"contrast":["low"],"language":["ca","cs","de","en","es","fr","hu","it","nl","pl","pt","sl","sv","tr"],"number_style":["uppercase"],"recommended_for":[],"weight":["heavy","light","regular"],"width":["regular"],"x_height":[]},"description":"Although at first sight Mashine is a strict, “non-designed” typeface, this display font is not as geometric as it seems. The use of serif-like terminals and unusual joints gives the design a unique look. For most letters, stylistic alternates can be accessed by using lowercase or capital letters.","foundry":"Just Another Foundry","lastModified":1588840823227,"name":"JAF Mashine Rounded","variations":["n2","n3","n4","n6","n7","n8"],"web_link":"http://typekit.com/fonts/jaf-mashine-rounded"},{"id":"sfpl"