at looks to the past for inspiration, but is a new contemporary design usable in a wide range of graphic settings. Le Havre is named for the port where many a famous luxury cruise liner was launched in the 1930s. ","foundry":"Insigne Design","lastModified":1588840823836,"name":"Le Havre ","variations":["n2","i2","n3","i3","n4","i4","n7","i7","n9","i9"],"web_link":"http://typekit.com/fonts/le-havre"},{"id":"mcxm","__v":0,"browse_info":{"capitals":["uppercase-lowercase"],"classification":["sans-serif"],"contrast":["regular"],"language":["ca","cs","de","en","es","fr","hu","it","mt","nl","pl","pt","sl","sv","tr"],"number_style":["uppercase"],"recommended_for":[],"weight":["heavy","light","regular"],"width":["condensed"],"x_height":["low"]},"description":"The Le Havre series is a series of geometric sans serifs inspired by the dignified era of the passenger ship, when getting to your destination was a delight in and of itself. Le Havre Rounded is a fun and new interpretation of geometric sans serifs. Le Havre Rounded features its sister family’s compressed capitals, low x-height and geometric construction, and its rounded forms lend it to be used in contemporary and technology settings. The Le Havre family includes a spectrum of weights for many design options.","foundry":"Insigne Design","lastModified":1588840823811,"name":"Le Havre Rounded","variations":["n2","i2","n3","i3","n4","i4","n7","i7","n8","i8"],"web_link":"http://typekit.com/fonts/le-havre-rounded"},{"id":"tnhw","__v":0,"browse_info":{"capitals":["uppercase-lowercase"],"classification":["serif"],"contrast":["regular"],"language":["ca","de","en","es","fr","it","nl","pt","sv"],"number_style":["lowercase"],"recommended_for":[],"weight":["heavy","regular"],"width":["regular"],"x_height":["high"]},"description":"Le Monde Courrier PTF, designed by Jean François Porchez, attempts to re-establish a style halfway between writing and printing.  It returns the informal character of “typewritten” fonts to letters and is well suited for printing in poor conditions such as faxes and low resolution printers.\r\n\r\n[See more weights of Le Monde Courrier Std](https://typekit.com/fonts/le-monde-courrier-std-2)","foundry":"Typofonderie","lastModified":1588840823840,"name":"Le Monde Courrier Std","variations":["n4","i4","n6","i6","n7","i7"],"web_link":"http://typekit.com/fonts/le-monde-courrier-std"},{"id":"cvjj","__v":0,"browse_info":{"capitals":["uppercase-lowercase"],"classification":["serif"],"contrast":["regular"],"language":["ca","de","en","es","fr","it","nl","pt","sv"],"number_style":["lowercase"],"recommended_for":[],"weight":["regular"],"width":["regular"],"x_height":["high"]},"description":null,"foundry":"Typofonderie","lastModified":1588840823822,"name":"Le Monde Courrier Std 2","variations":["n4","i4"],"web_link":"http://typekit.com/fonts/le-monde-courrier-std-2"},{"id":"mvgb","__v":0,"browse_info":{"capitals":["uppercase-lowercase"],"classification":["serif"],"contrast":["high"],"language":["ca","de","en","es","fr","it","nl","pt","sv"],"number_style":["uppercase"],"recommended_for":[],"weight":["heavy","regular"],"width":["regular"],"x_height":["high"]},"description":"Le Monde Journal is the typeface on which the entire Le Monde family is based. By definition, it is intended for newspaper use & at small sizes. This family was designed in 1994 as custom font for the French newspaper Le Monde. The family has not been used by the newspaper since 2005, though you do still see it in sister publications from time to time. \r\n\r\n[See more weights](https://typekit.com/fonts/le-monde-sans-std-2)\r\n\r\n[See more weights](https://typekit.com/fonts/le-monde-journal-std-2)","foundry":"Typofonderie","lastModified":1588840823848,"name":"Le Monde Journal Std","variations":["n4","i4","n6","i6","n7","i7"],"web_link":"http://typekit.com/fonts/le-monde-journal-std"},{"id":"dvrn","__v":0,"browse_info":{"capitals":["uppercase-lowercase"],"classification":["serif"],"contrast":["regular"],"language":["ca","de","en","es","fr","it","nl","pt","sv"],"number_style":["lowercase"],"recommended_for":[],"weight":["regular"],"width":["regular"],"x_height":["high"]},"description":null,"foundry":"Typofonderie","lastModified":1588840823827,"name":"Le Monde Journal Std 2","variations":["n4","i4"],"web_link":"http://typekit.com/fonts/le-monde-journal-std-2"},{"id":"wxzn","__v":0,"browse_info":{"capitals":["uppercase-lowercase"],"classification":["serif"],"contrast":["regular"],"language":["ca","de","en","es","fr","it","nl","pt","sv"],"number_style":["lowercase"],"recommended_for":[],"weight":["regular"],"width":["regular"],"x_height":["high"]},"description":"See more styles: [Le Monde Livre Classic Std SC](https://typekit.com/fonts/le-monde-livre-classic-std-sc), [Le Monde Livre Classic Std Swash](https://typekit.com/fonts/le-monde-livre-classic-std-swash)","foundry":"Typofonderie","lastModified":1588840823857,"name":"Le Monde Livre Classic Std","variations":["n3","i3","n4","n5","n7"],"web_link":"http://typekit.com/fonts/le-monde-livre-classic-byol"},{"id":"shhb","__v":0,"browse_info":{"capitals":["uppercase-lowercase"],"classification":["serif"],"contrast":["regular"],"language":["ca","de","en","es","fr","it","nl","pt","sv"],"number_style":["lowercase"],"recommended_for":[],"weight":["light","regular"],"width":["regular"],"x_height":["regular"]},"description":null,"foundry":"Typofonderie","lastModified":1588840823862,"name":"Le Monde Livre Std","variations":["n3","i3","n4","i4","n5","i5","n7","i7"],"web_link":"http://typekit.com/fonts/le-monde-livre-std"},{"id":"rshz","__v":0,"browse_info":{"capitals":["uppercase-lowercase"],"classification":["sans-serif"],"contrast":["regular"],"language":["ca","de","en","es","fr","it","nl","pt","sv"],"number_style":["uppercase"],"recommended_for":[],"weight":["regular"],"width":["regular"],"x_height":["high"]},"description":"Designed by Jean François Porchez, Le Monde Sans PTF is a lineal type family—one which has been derived from serifed types.  The design of Le Monde Sans PTF continues the basic common structure found in the members of the Le Monde family: its proportions, a relatively narrow width, a fairly oblique axis, etc. The typographer can, at all times, switch between Sans Ptf & Journal Ptf or Courrier Ptf without any disruption in the composition.\r\n\r\n[See more weights](https://typekit.com/fonts/le-monde-sans-std-2)","foundry":"Typofonderie","lastModified":1675386684926,"name":"Le Monde Sans Std","variations":["n2","i2","n3","i3","n4","i4","n6","i6","n7","i7","n8","i8"],"web_link":"http://typekit.com/fonts/le-monde-sans-std"},{"id":"lcdz","__v":0,"browse_info":{"capitals":["uppercase-lowercase"],"classification":["sans-serif"],"contrast":["regular"],"language":["ca","de","en","es","fr","it","nl","pt","sv"],"number_style":["lowercase"],"recommended_for":[],"weight":["regular"],"width":["regular"],"x_height":["high"]},"description":null,"foundry":"Typofonderie","lastModified":1588840823870,"name":"Le Monde Sans Std 2","variations":["n5","i5"],"web_link":"http://typekit.com/fonts/le-monde-sans-std-2"},{"id":"kmpm","__v":0,"browse_info":{"capitals":["uppercase-lowercase"],"classification":["sans-serif"],"contrast":["regular"],"language":["cs","en","es","hu","mt","nl","pt","sl","sv","tr"],"number_style":["uppercase"],"recommended_for":["headings"],"weight":["regular"],"width":["condensed"],"x_height":["high"]},"description":"League Gothic is our revival of an old classic, and one of our favorite typefaces, Alternate Gothic No.1. It was originally designed by Morris Fuller Benton for the American Type Founders Company (ATF) in 1903. The company went bankrupt in 1993. And since the original typeface was created before 1923, the typeface is in the public domain.","foundry":"The League of Moveable Type","lastModified":1588840823875,"name":"League Gothic","variations":["n4","i4"],"web_link":"http://typekit.com/fonts/league-gothic"},{"id":"wvpq","__v":0,"browse_info":{"capitals":["uppercase-l