yyc","__v":0,"browse_info":{"capitals":["uppercase-lowercase"],"classification":["sans-serif"],"contrast":["regular"],"language":["ca","cs","de","en","es","fr","hu","it","mt","nl","pl","pt","sl","sv","tr"],"number_style":["uppercase"],"recommended_for":[],"weight":["heavy","light","regular"],"width":["regular"],"x_height":["high"]},"description":"Project a powerful image with Sommet. Sommet is a sans-serif with a high-tech web 2.0 feel. The typeface family is a powerful and sharp design that is highly legible onscreen even at small sizes. Sommet features a tall x-height, and its letterforms are compressed, perfect for when layout space is at a premium. The Sommet family includes four weights and italics for plenty of design options and is suitable for body copy and display text.","foundry":"Insigne Design","lastModified":1740095523762,"name":"Sommet","variations":["n1","i1","n3","i3","n4","i4","n7","i7","n8","i8","n9","i9"],"web_link":"http://fonts.adobe.com/fonts/sommet"},{"id":"gqfn","__v":0,"browse_info":{"capitals":["uppercase-lowercase"],"classification":["sans-serif"],"contrast":["regular"],"language":["ca","cs","de","en","es","fr","hu","it","mt","nl","pl","pt","ru","sl","sv","tr"],"number_style":["uppercase"],"recommended_for":[],"weight":["heavy","light","regular"],"width":["regular"],"x_height":["high"]},"description":"The Sommet series has been updated with a rounded variant. Sommet Rounded retains its predecessor's high-tech web 2.0 character but features blunted terminators, making for a much warmer and friendlier impression. Sommet Rounded features a tall x-height, and its letterforms are compressed, perfect for when layout space is at a premium. Sommet Rounded can be easily mixed and matched with its non-rounded relative. Sommet Rounded includes four weights and italics for plenty of design options and is suitable for body copy and display text. In 2009 Sommet Rounded was updated to include Cyrillic support.","foundry":"Insigne Design","lastModified":1588840829997,"name":"Sommet Rounded","variations":["n1","i1","n3","i3","n4","i4","n7","i7","n8","i8","n9","i9"],"web_link":"http://typekit.com/fonts/sommet-rounded"},{"id":"qlvb","__v":0,"browse_info":{"capitals":["uppercase-lowercase"],"classification":["slab-serif"],"contrast":["regular"],"language":["ca","cs","de","en","es","fr","hu","it","mt","nl","pl","pt","sl","sv","tr"],"number_style":["uppercase"],"recommended_for":[],"weight":["heavy","light","regular"],"width":["regular"],"x_height":["high"]},"description":"Expanding on Sommet’s successful design principals, Sommet Slab is there when you need more impact and power. Sommet Slab features a tall x-height, and its letterforms are compact, perfect for when layout space is at a premium. Use Sommet Slab whenever you need a powerful and contemporary slab-serif.","foundry":"Insigne Design","lastModified":1588840829991,"name":"Sommet Slab","variations":["n1","i1","n3","i3","n4","i4","n7","i7","n8","i8","n9","i9"],"web_link":"http://typekit.com/fonts/sommet-slab"},{"id":"kwmd","__v":0,"browse_info":{"capitals":["uppercase-lowercase"],"classification":["slab-serif"],"contrast":["regular"],"language":["ca","cs","de","en","es","fr","hu","it","mt","nl","pl","pt","sl","sv","tr"],"number_style":["uppercase"],"recommended_for":[],"weight":["regular"],"width":["regular"],"x_height":["high"]},"description":"Sommet Slab Titling Caps contains alternate (titling) capital letters for Sommet Slab.","foundry":"Insigne Design","lastModified":1588840829979,"name":"Sommet Slab Titling Caps","variations":["n4","i4","n7","i7"],"web_link":"http://typekit.com/fonts/sommet-slab-titling-caps"},{"id":"nzln","__v":0,"browse_info":{"capitals":[],"classification":[],"contrast":[],"language":[],"number_style":[],"recommended_for":[],"weight":[],"width":[],"x_height":[]},"description":null,"foundry":"Famira Fonts","lastModified":1633569069165,"name":"Sonar Sans","variations":["n3","i3","n4","i4","n5","i5","n6","i6","n7","i7","n8","i8"],"web_link":"http://typekit.com/fonts/sonar-sans"},{"id":"npbj","__v":0,"browse_info":{"capitals":["all-or-small-caps"],"classification":["decorative"],"contrast":["regular"],"language":[],"number_style":["uppercase"],"recommended_for":[],"weight":["regular"],"width":["regular"],"x_height":[]},"description":null,"foundry":"Carter & Cone","lastModified":1667956279376,"name":"Sophia CC","variations":["n4"],"web_link":"http://typekit.com/fonts/sophia-cc"},{"id":"nnzs","__v":0,"browse_info":{"capitals":["uppercase-lowercase"],"classification":["sans-serif"],"contrast":["low"],"language":["ca","de","en","es","fr","it","nl","pt","sv"],"number_style":["uppercase"],"recommended_for":[],"weight":["heavy","light","regular"],"width":["regular"],"x_height":["regular"]},"description":"The sturdy Sophisto comes in five weights, each with italics, and is accompanied by a set of small caps. Sophisto is rigid, but not uniform: it contains some unexpected angles and curves, like in the similar forms found in the cap K, R, and P, as well as in the asymmetrical O. The italics offer just a touch of softness in an otherwise hard typeface, with ever-so-slightly curved in- and outstrokes.","foundry":"MAC Rhino Fonts","lastModified":1588840830009,"name":"Sophisto","variations":["n1","i1","n3","i3","n4","i4","n7","i7","n9","i9"],"web_link":"http://typekit.com/fonts/sophisto"},{"id":"xhsp","__v":0,"browse_info":{"capitals":["all-or-small-caps"],"classification":["sans-serif"],"contrast":["low"],"language":["ca","de","en","es","fr","it","nl","pt","sv"],"number_style":["lowercase"],"recommended_for":[],"weight":["light","regular"],"width":["regular"],"x_height":["regular"]},"description":"The sturdy Sophisto comes in five weights, each with italics, and is accompanied by a set of small caps. Sophisto is rigid, but not uniform: it contains some unexpected angles and curves, like in the similar forms found in the cap K, R, and P, as well as in the asymmetrical O. The italics offer just a touch of softness in an otherwise hard typeface, with ever-so-slightly curved in- and outstrokes.","foundry":"MAC Rhino Fonts","lastModified":1588840830033,"name":"Sophisto SC","variations":["n1","n3","n4"],"web_link":"http://typekit.com/fonts/sophisto-sc-osf"},{"id":"yrwy","__v":0,"browse_info":{"capitals":["uppercase-lowercase"],"classification":["serif"],"contrast":["regular"],"language":["ca","cs","de","en","es","fr","hu","it","mt","nl","pl","pt","sl","sv","tr"],"number_style":["lowercase"],"recommended_for":[],"weight":["regular"],"width":["regular"],"x_height":["regular"]},"description":"A ‘revival’ of Goudy Oldstyle and Italic with  oldstyle and lining figures, superscripts and subscripts, fractions, ligatures, class-based kerning, case-sensitive forms, and capital spacing.","foundry":"The League of Moveable Type","lastModified":1588840830014,"name":"Sorts Mill Goudy","variations":["n5","i5"],"web_link":"http://typekit.com/fonts/sorts-mill-goudy"},{"id":"fprg","__v":0,"browse_info":{"capitals":[],"classification":[],"contrast":[],"language":[],"number_style":[],"recommended_for":[],"weight":[],"width":[],"x_height":[]},"description":null,"foundry":"Google","is_personal":false,"lastModified":1734108736304,"name":"Sour Gummy","variations":["n1","i1","n2","i2","n3","i3","n4","i4","n5","i5","n6","i6","n7","i7","n8","i8","n9","i9"],"web_link":"http://fonts.adobe.com/fonts/sour-gummy"},{"id":"kmqc","__v":0,"browse_info":{"capitals":[],"classification":[],"contrast":[],"language":[],"number_style":[],"recommended_for":[],"weight":[],"width":[],"x_height":[]},"description":null,"foundry":"Google","is_personal":false,"lastModified":1734108736331,"name":"Sour Gummy Expanded","variations":["n1","i1","n2","i2","n3","i3","n4","i4","n5","i5","n6","i6","n7","i7","n8","i8","n9","i9"],"web_link":"http://fonts.adobe.com/fonts/sour-gummy-expanded"},{"id":"tjpp","__v":0,"browse_info":{"capitals":[],"classification":[],"contrast":[],"language":[],"number_style":[],"recommended_for":[],"weight":[],"width":[],"x_height":[]},"description":null,"foundry":"Google","is_personal":false,"lastModified":1734108736318,"name":"Sour Gummy SemiExpanded","variations":["n1","i1","n2","i2","n3","i3","n4","i4","n5","i5","n6","i6","n7","i7","n8","i8","n9","i9"],"web_link":"http://fonts.adobe.com/fonts/sour-gummy-semiexpanded"},{"id":"dkxf","__v":0,"browse_info":{"capitals":["uppercase-lowercase"],"classification":["monospaced"],"contrast":["low"],"language":["ca","cs","de","el","en","es","fr","hu","it","mt","nl","pl","pt","ru","sl","sv","tr","vi"],"number_style":["uppercase"],"recommended_for":[],"weight":["heavy","light","regular"],"width":["regular"],"x_height":["regular"]},"description":"Source Code Pro was designed by [Paul D. Hunt](http://www.adobe.com/products/type/font-designers/paul-hunt.html) as a companion to [Source Sans](https://typekit.com/fonts/source-sans-pro).\r\n\r\nThis complementary family was adapted from the Source design to create a monospaced version for coding applications. Source Code preserves the design features and vertical proportions of Source Sans, but alters the glyph widths so that they are uniform across all glyphs and weights. Although a regular weight will typically suffice for coding environments, Source Code is available in the same weight range as the corresponding Source Sans design.\r\n\r\nSource Code Pro currently supports a wide range of languages using the Latin script. The latest release adds support for Greek and Cyrillic scripts (upright fonts only) and italics.","foundry":"Adobe Originals","lastModified":1588840830063,"name":"Source Code Pro","variations":["n2","i2","n3","i3","n4","i4","n5","i5","n6","i6","n7","i7","n9","i9"],"web_link":"http://typekit.com/fonts/source-code-pro"},{"id":"ckcb","__v":0,"browse_info":{"capitals":["uppercase-lowercase"],"classification":["sans-serif"],"contrast":["low"],"language":[],"number_style":["uppercase"],"recommended_for":["headings","paragraphs"],"weight":["heavy","light","regular"],"width":["regular"],"x_height":["high"]},"description":null,"foundry":"Adobe Originals","lastModified":1680311487415,"name":"Source Sans 3","variations":["n2","i2","n3","i3","n4","i4","n5","i5","n6","i6","n7","i7","n9","i9"],"web_link":"http://typekit.com/fonts/source-sans-3"},{"id":"bhyf","__v":0,"browse_info":{"capitals":["uppercase-lowercase"],"classification":["sans-serif"],"contrast":["regular"],"language":["ca","cs","de","el","en","es","fr","hu","it","mt","nl","pl","pt","ru","sl","sv","tr","vi"],"number_style":["uppercase"],"recommended_for":["headings","paragraphs"],"weight":["heavy","light","regular"],"width":["regular"],"x_height":["high"]},"description":"Source Sans Pro was designed by [Paul D. Hunt](http://www.adobe.com/products/type/font-designers/paul-hunt.html) under the guidance of [Robert Slimbach](http://www.adobe.com/products/type/font-designers/robert-slimbach.html). It is Adobe's first open source typeface family, conceived primarily as a typeface for user interfaces. Source Sans Pro draws inspiration from the clarity and legibility of twentieth-century American gothic typeface designs. Distilling the best archetypical qualities of these models, Paul followed a rational design approach by simplifying glyph shapes by paring them to their essential form. However, in order to more easily differentiate similar letter shapes (such as uppercase I and lowercase L), some additional details have been added. Besides providing such explicitly clarity in short text strings, another fundamental design consideration was to create a typeface that reads well in extended settings. This can be seen in the general proportions: Source Sans Pro has been designed with a more generous width than many other comparable gothics, and its shorter majuscule letters, combined with minuscule letters with longer extenders, create a more pleasant reading texture in longer text passages.\r\n\r\nSource Sans Pro currently supports a wide range of languages using Latin script. Additionally, this family supports modern and polytonic Greek and features coverage for extended Cyrillic. Other members of the greater Source type system include [Source Code Pro](https://typekit.com/fonts/source-code-pro), a monospaced version of Source Sans designed specifically for coding, and [Source Serif Pro](https://typekit.com/fonts/source-serif-pro).","foundry":"Adobe Originals","lastModified":1588840830039,"name":"Source Sans Pro","variations":["n2","i2","n3","i3","n4","i4","n6","i6","n7","i7","n9","i9"],"web_link":"http://typekit.com/fonts/source-sans-pro"},{"id":"lxbc","__v":0,"browse_info":{"capitals":["uppercase-lowercase"],"classification":["serif"],"contrast":["regular"],"language":[],"number_style":["uppercase"],"recommended_for":[],"weight":["heavy","light","regular"],"width":["regular"],"x_height":["regular"]},"description":null,"foundry":"Adobe Originals","lastModified":1614215457792,"name":"Source Serif 4","variations":["n2","i2","n3","i3","n4","i4","n6","i6","n7","i7","n9","i9"],"web_link":"http://typekit.com/fonts/source-serif-4"},{"id":"zdpf","__v":0,"browse_info":{"capitals":["uppercase-lowercase"],"classification":["serif"],"contrast":["regular"],"language":[],"number_style":["uppercase"],"recommended_for":[],"weight":["heavy","light","regular"],"width":["regular"],"x_height":["regular"]},"description":null,"foundry":"Adobe Originals","lastModified":1614215457764,"name":"Source Serif 4 Caption","variations":["n2","i2","n3","i3","n4","i4","n6","i6","n7","i7","n9","i9"],"web_link":"http://typekit.com/fonts/source-serif-4-caption"},{"id":"rlfy","__v":0,"browse_info":{"capitals":["uppercase-lowercase"],"classification":["serif"],"contrast":["regular"],"language":[],"number_style":["uppercase"],"recommended_for":[],"weight":["heavy","light","regular"],"width":["regular"],"x_height":["regular"]},"description":null,"foundry":"Adobe Originals","lastModified":1614215457783,"name":"Source Serif 4 Display","variations":["n2","i2","n3","i3","n4","i4","n6","i6","n7"