e":"Tephra","variations":["n1","n3","n4","n5","n6","n7"],"web_link":"http://typekit.com/fonts/tephra"},{"id":"yhln","__v":0,"browse_info":{"capitals":["uppercase-lowercase"],"classification":["sans-serif"],"contrast":["low"],"language":["ca","cs","de","en","es","fr","hu","it","mt","nl","pl","pt","sl","sv","tr"],"number_style":["uppercase"],"recommended_for":[],"weight":["light","regular"],"width":["regular"],"x_height":["high"]},"description":"Terfens is a sans serif with inspiration from chancery scripts like Stefania. Subtly rounded and eschewing harsh technical lines, Terfens is a warm and inviting typeface. Its tall x-height gives it a friendly but not overly informal feel. Its readability and unique contemporary look makes it suitable for a wide range of design applications.","foundry":"Insigne Design","lastModified":1588840831062,"name":"Terfens","variations":["n1","i1","n3","i3","n4","i4","n5","i5","n7","i7","n9","i9"],"web_link":"http://typekit.com/fonts/terfens"},{"id":"rqxw","__v":0,"browse_info":{"capitals":["uppercase-lowercase"],"classification":["sans-serif"],"contrast":["regular"],"language":[],"number_style":["uppercase"],"recommended_for":["headings"],"weight":["heavy","light","regular"],"width":["extended"],"x_height":["high"]},"description":null,"foundry":"Fort Foundry","lastModified":1588840831033,"name":"Termina","variations":["n1","n2","n3","n4","n5","n6","n7","n8","n9"],"web_link":"http://typekit.com/fonts/termina"},{"id":"qbct","__v":0,"browse_info":{"capitals":["uppercase-lowercase"],"classification":["decorative"],"contrast":["low"],"language":["ca","de","en","es","fr","it","nl","pt","sv"],"number_style":["lowercase"],"recommended_for":[],"weight":["regular"],"width":["regular"],"x_height":[]},"description":"TwentyFourNinetyOne [2491] is a reinterpretation of the alphabet of 1919 by Theo van Doesburg; the original a true rendering of the thinking of the Dutch-based art movement “de Stijl,” horizontals and verticals that inspired and synced with the work of Piet Mondrian (1872-1944), Gerrit Rietveld (1888-1964), Vilmos Huszár (1884-1960), J.J.P. Oud (1890-1963) and others; planting the seed that would become the modernist “look” of the 20th century.\r\nJump forward to 1980 and prop lettering used on the “Buck Rogers in the 25th Century” television series; a vernacular typeface that was a utilitarian mix of geometry and pixel-based forms, used to symbolize the futuristic universe of 2491. At times it would appear on spaceships, laser guns, signage at space ports or in one episode, a Spandex tapestry.\r\n\r\nIt only seemed logical to combine and rethink the letterforms, add ligatures + other extras, and see what the results would be. Futuristic, fun and bold to read!\r\n\r\n2491: In the future, all type will look like this.","foundry":"Steve Mehallo","lastModified":1588840831044,"name":"TewentyFourNinetyOne","variations":["n4"],"web_link":"http://typekit.com/fonts/tewentyfourninetyone"},{"id":"vvpx","__v":0,"browse_info":{"capitals":["uppercase-lowercase"],"classification":["script"],"contrast":["regular"],"language":["ca","cs","de","en","es","fr","hu","it","mt","nl","pl","pt","sl","sv","tr"],"number_style":["lowercase"],"recommended_for":["headings"],"weight":["regular"],"width":["regular"],"x_height":["low"]},"description":null,"foundry":"Three Islands Press","lastModified":1588840831021,"name":"Texas Hero","variations":["n4"],"web_link":"http://typekit.com/fonts/texas-hero"},{"id":"dxlb","__v":0,"browse_info":{"capitals":["uppercase-lowercase"],"classification":["sans-serif"],"contrast":["low"],"language":["ca","cs","de","en","es","fr","hu","it","mt","nl","pl","pt","ru","sl","sv","tr"],"number_style":["uppercase"],"recommended_for":[],"weight":["heavy","light","regular"],"width":["regular"],"x_height":["regular"]},"description":"Designed for ParaType in 2007 by Isabella Chaeva. It was developed for primers and the first level school textbooks. An early sans serif ('Grotesque') with half-closed static 